peers ListAgents at lap open named grain-d3, a Claude session on this machine, started an hour before; a note was sent naming this lap's lane and files before anything moved (REDS %291 habit). It landed 573853d97 on tools/fixtures/chatgpt_mind_loop_control.sh mid-roster, which is this lap's tree_moved=yes and touched none of these paths.
title the needle the harness supplied -- the parked glow_gate_answer ratchet adopted, and one wall that could never red
prompt Open as SILENCE under the INNER LOOP Standing block -- roster cold then hot, reds first as standfast, QA on touch, the council rota row N mod 5, prose witnesses on prose sends, stamp-and-name, ASCII-first, READ SCOPE -- then pick up the running thread and take the infrastructure-Glow lane.
think The running thread named this lap by name. Sound's 20260828.110207 log closes with "the parked glow_gate_answer ratchet remains Silence's half, counting the remaining contains-shaped walls tree-wide when its lap adopts the park", and REDS %310 says the same in its Kin line. So the lap was booked before it opened; the work was to find out what the park actually measures.
think First reading was too coarse and I threw it away. Grepping contains across tools/*.rish returns 1,669 files of 1,911 -- the whole witness surface, which measures nothing. Narrowing to short needles gave 482 lines in 90 files, still not a fault: a short needle is not wrong, it is short.
think The fault is narrower and it has a mechanism. A witness captures a lowered binary as run ["sh" "-c" "${bin}; echo EXIT:$?"], so the echo fires unconditionally and EXIT:<code> stands in .out whether the binary spoke or not. Any contains needle that is a substring of that framing -- "0", "1", "EXIT", "EXIT:", ":" -- is satisfied before the program is consulted. That is exactly what %310 caught: EXIT:0 feeding contains "0".
think Second reading, also thrown away: I counted a run whose only assertions are .ok and contains "EXIT:0" as blind, and got 151 across 34 files. Reading glow_lower_cell_witness.rish showed why that overcounts -- welcome exits 0, unwelcome exits 1, both asserted, and the exit code IS the claim. A two-sided exit wall is an honest wall.
think Third reading is the one that holds, and it splits by what a guard can be. Two GATES at zero, because both read zero once one line is repaired: a needle the framing alone supplies, and a run captured and never asserted at all. Two RATCHETS under falling ceilings, because they are not-yet-uniform rather than wrong: 152 answer-blind runs, and 7 files that assert a clean exit and never once, by any spelling, a refusal. The Fire row's own words for the split -- a red is something wrong, a ratchet merely turns on touch.
think The scan found a hit I had missed by hand. glow_lower_assert_witness.rish:40 read assert run_un.out contains "EXIT:" -- the harness prints EXIT: always, so that wall could never red. I had already grepped those same 35 files twice looking for exactly this class and walked past it, because I was reading for bare digits and this needle is five characters of the framing itself.
think My own grep also miscounted the never-refused files at 8, because glow_lower_assert_witness.rish:41 spells its refusal as assert (run_un.out contains "EXIT:0") == false, a form no EXIT:[1-9] pattern reaches. The scan reads that as a refusal and the honest count is 7. Both corrections came from writing the meter rather than from looking harder.
obs The repair is subtraction into the family's own shape, the same move %310 made. Line 40 becomes assert run_un.ok, which is verbatim what lines 27 and 33 of that same file already say, and the honest negated refusal on line 41 stands untouched. Nothing was added; a vacuous line was replaced by the one its siblings already use.
obs Both ceilings are proven from both sides by planting one past them, so no override exists and none is wanted. The blind ceiling is proven by generating a file with ceiling+1 runs; the file-counted ceiling needed report mode to accept many files, which it now does -- a wall with a door beside it is a habit again, and an env-var override would have been that door.
obs The pen cites the ceilings off the scan's own output rather than spelling them again, so deleting one makes the control refuse rather than guess. Same discipline the QA card uses when it lifts measure() out of the register scan.
obs What this does not reach, written into the scan's header rather than left to be found: whether an asserted answer is the RIGHT answer, and whether a witness proving its LOWERING refuses counts -- glow_lower_shop_gate_witness.rish proves SampleDoesNotNest in its selftest and still stands in never_refused_files, because that is the compiler refusing, not the lowered binary. Word presence is the check; a reader is the standard.
obs The two ratchets are honestly not mine to close. 34 of the 152 sit in glow_lower_shop_gate_witness.rish, whose binaries include ${argv_bin} 9 -- the argv shape %310 caught exiting clean and silent -- and reading their answer needs the plants to speak, which is a lowering change under Sound's language custody. Named in the row, the card, and the roster comment rather than quietly carried.
obs The cold roster took 30 minutes and read tree_moved=yes, because grain-d3 committed 573853d97 while it ran. Its two reds are both known: declared_ceiling is REDS %295, Mind's and gated, and remember_git_nib is the card's stale nib, which this lap's own send closes. No new tree red opened.
obs The card is at 24,575 bytes against a 24,576 bound -- one byte of headroom after four trims of my own paragraph. It stood at 24,566 at HEAD, so the pressure predates this lap; a card permanently at its ceiling wants its own fold round, and that is a line rather than a red.
obs REDS folded within its own day again. %310 was the only closed flat row and the pin was 679 over, so it went to construction/archive/REDS-the-gate-that-proved-itself-rows-310.md with a recital row. Its kin %311 stays flat and open -- both rows describe one thing from two sides.
obs The rota read row 2, Fire/Mars, cut and stop, sense of vision: the threshold plus standfast cardinal, reds-first fixed, the three depths dual. N is git rev-list --count HEAD at 3602 and 3602 mod 5 is 2; the previous Silence lap read Aether, so no repeat and no hand-advance. The fixed seat governed the lap -- a red is something wrong, a ratchet merely turns on touch -- and the cardinal gave it its shape: a lantern that fires twice becomes a loom, where %310 was the lantern.
loom witness=glow_gate_answer wall_s=3 scan_s=1 control_s=1 witness_files=35 laundered=0 answer_blind=152 never_refused=7 control_cases=22
loom roster=cold guards_run=75 guards_green=73 guards_red=2 wall_min=30 tree_moved=yes
